From ddd22ece3bf21a1fea9808f9a9eae79dacec7bd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:02:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 190/191] EE timers: advanced in one piece up to the next timer
 interrupt; GIF_STAT slot looked up once

PS2Memory::advanceEeTimers runs at every branch the EE takes. Each call looked GIF_STAT up in the register hash map
and did two 64-bit multiply-divides per running timer: 7-9 % of the game thread in a movie on a Steam Deck
(measured; nearly all of it the timer arithmetic).

- GIF_STAT's slot in m_ioRegisters is remembered (dropped when the map is cleared or its owner destroyed).
- Timer deferral: a timer's count is a pure function of the cycles since it was last written, so calls are summed
  and applied in one piece when the sum reaches the first cycle at which a timer interrupt is raised (the exact
  horizon cyclesUntilNextEeTimerInterrupt already computes for the idle wait), and before any timer register is read
  or written. The interrupt is raised by the same call as before.
- GA2_EE_TIMER_DEFER=0 turns it off; =check advances a shadow copy call by call and aborts if the timers ever differ
  from it, or if an interrupt was due inside a horizon.

The state lives in ps2_memory.cpp (keyed by its PS2Memory), not in the class: ps2_memory.h is precompiled into the
game code and stays untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
